---

<BlogArticleShell
  title="Kakobuy Spreadsheet sizing: Taobao &amp; Weidian charts, shoe conversions, and QC expectation-setting | kakobuy-cn.com"
  description="Long-tail sizing literacy for Kakobuy Spreadsheet buyers—decode CN apparel tables, cm foot traces vs EU/US sneaker sizes, measurement photos before warehouse QC, plus links to Taobao/Weidian paste guides."
  canonicalPath={canonicalPath}
  headline="Kakobuy Spreadsheet sizing: Taobao &amp; Weidian charts, shoe conversions, and QC expectation-setting"
  publishedISO={publishedISO}
  displayDate="13 May 2026"
  structuredKeywords={[
    'Kakobuy Spreadsheet sizing',
    'Taobao size chart cm',
    'Weidian shoe sizing EU',
    'CN sizing conversion spreadsheet',
    'Kakobuy QC measurements clothes',
    'international shoe cm foot length',
  ]}
>
  <p class="blog-lede" slot="lede">
    Spreadsheet thumbnails rarely embed <strong>grading tables</strong>—yet disputes spike when shoulder widths or insole centimetres mismatch fantasy fits.
    Because Kakobuy forwards what sellers ship, sizing literacy upstream beats screenshot apologies downstream.
    This guide connects marketplace chart reading with warehouse QC habits already outlined in our <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-qc/">QC primer</a>, without pretending kakobuy-cn.com tailors garments remotely.
  </p>

  <h2>Decode the usual Taobao-style chart columns</h2>
  <p>
    Seller tables typically mix <strong>衣长 / 胸围 / 肩宽</strong> (length, bust, shoulder) in centimetres, occasionally layering &ldquo;建议体重&rdquo; weight bands meant for domestic shoppers—ignore those bands for muscular or tall frames abroad.
    Always locate whether measurements assume <strong>flat garment</strong> or <strong>body circumference</strong>; confused bloggers routinely compare incomparable labels.
    Pair this discipline with stable listing URLs from <a href="/blog/kakobuy-taobao/">Taobao paste hygiene</a> so variant IDs referencing &ldquo;Size 2/M&rdquo; still match the chart row you screenshot before paying agents.
  </p>

  <h2>Weidian albums &amp; ambiguity budgets</h2>
  <p>
    Micro-stores sometimes hide charts inside carousel slides or worse—seller chat screenshots—so Spreadsheet rows deserve explicit notes referencing <em>which album revision</em> blessed your pick.
    Refer back to <a href="/blog/kakobuy-weidian/">Weidian URL drift guide</a>; sizing disputes spike when albums silently refresh silhouettes while URLs appear unchanged.
  </p>

  <h2>Sneaker sizing without mythology</h2>
  <p>
    CN listings frequently cite <strong>脚长 cm</strong> (foot trace length) mapped to arbitrary EU/US stamps that batch factories reinterpret each season.
    Workflow that survives QC:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>Trace both feet on paper wearing intended socks; measure longest axis in millimetres.</li>
    <li>Compare against seller cm ladder—not hype resale charts from Reddit albums.</li>
    <li>Add tolerance for toe stiffeners on boots versus knit runners.</li>
    <li>Ask sellers for insole length photos when charts omit vertical depth data.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    When warehouse photography arrives, overlay expectation quickly using grid overlays described philosophically in <a href="/blog/qc-websites-landscape/">QC tooling landscape</a>—community montages never substitute for Kakobuy inbound captures attached to your order line.
  </p>

  <h2>Spreadsheet annotation habits that scale</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Dual units:</strong> log both seller-native cm and your localized preference beside each row ID—future-you avoids frantic Discord archaeology.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Layer counts:</strong> note padded jackets versus tees when interpreting bust measurements; insulation steals interior circumference.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Revision hash:</strong> paste lightweight checksum (ISO date + screenshot filename) proving which chart governed checkout timing—pairs nicely with warehouse timelines from <a href="/blog/kakobuy-warehouse-storage-spreadsheet/">warehouse storage article</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Where Kakobuy still cannot rescue bad guesses</h2>
  <p>
    Agents measure parcels—not bodies—and QC imagery showcases factory output, not bespoke tailoring.
    If sellers omit tolerance bands entirely, accept elevated rejection risk or pivot listings before domestic fulfilment locks yuan spends you regret later during parcel consolidation math tied to <a href="/blog/kakobuy-spreadsheet-to-parcel-checklist/">parcel checklist</a>.
  </p>

